 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Then an easier to use regular keyboard is perfect for you. Stick with one hand per button digeridoo style, or go right hand for faster typing. Then a small tablet can fit in a pocket, and you can use one hand each way. Which do you hate more, trackpads or keyboards? Then look at the larger models, they' usually the ones with decent pads. If you going to buy a new one within the next few months, consider a full size keyboard too. Then look at the cheaper models, they' usually better than mid priced ones. Try to find keyboard you' comfortable with, and use it. Most people switch between right hand only and one hand per button, depending on what they' doing.",
